{"data": [{"author_id": "2102064626099699713", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:15:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120309332843594174"], "id": "2120309332843594174", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Extended verification loops is the line I care about. For code driven video the model has to render a frame look at it and fix only the timestamp that broke. If Carbon closes that loop on Three.js or Remotion it changes how motion work gets made", "url": "https://x.com/Ian18858863/status/2120309332843594174"}, {"author_id": "1664916049995743232", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:09:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120307776123703578"], "id": "2120307776123703578", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@RapidataAI @GoogleDeepMind Carbon topping the 3D board is the number that matters for builders. a scene that holds together beats a pretty first render. does the lead hold on multi-turn edits, or mostly single-shot scenes?", "url": "https://x.com/astierun/status/2120307776123703578"}, {"author_id": "2100257555477868544", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:41:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120300911956500751"], "id": "2120300911956500751", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Thirteen days from \"cyber defenders only\" to \"start building.\" Good. Now let outside teams rerun that 88.2% SEC-bench Pro score, and test it on your own repos before the $2/$10 intro price doubles.", "url": "https://x.com/AIEarlyEdition/status/2120300911956500751"}, {"author_id": "343877206", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:11:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120293243103690931"], "id": "2120293243103690931", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Excited to try it on longer tasks. Thanks for the clear docs.", "url": "https://x.com/smobilefactory/status/2120293243103690931"}, {"author_id": "2020606799486013440", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:08:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120292430331437215"], "id": "2120292430331437215", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Any Ai worst than @GeminiApp Name it \n\nGem rubbish, Ai usage crap, Ai models slow and substandard,policies complete anti consumer, cloud services not available, deep research generic and ends on mind/cognitive behaviour I can bet so scam, new models available? no waste of money.", "url": "https://x.com/SYEDHASSAN41031/status/2120292430331437215"}, {"author_id": "2104993200490393600", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:07:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120292183173431759"], "id": "2120292183173431759", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Long-horizon is what actually matters. A model that's brilliant for 10 minutes is a demo. One that keeps checking its own work for 3 hours is something you can actually put to work.", "url": "https://x.com/ceobrendan/status/2120292183173431759"}, {"author_id": "1627059878710890500", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:59:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120290157433880595"], "id": "2120290157433880595", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@mianoedwin_ @GoogleDeepMind i've not tested 5.2 yet but that cost per task is a pretty ridiculous spike https://t.co/xiLzyJ41Xz", "url": "https://x.com/macblackstuff/status/2120290157433880595"}, {"author_id": "2109231484767031296", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:56:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120289561679163612"], "id": "2120289561679163612", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind @GeminiApp Finding vulnerabilities with sustained reasoning cuts both ways — the same capability that audits code can also be pointed at it. The interesting question isn't the reasoning depth, it's who gets access and under what disclosure rules.", "url": "https://x.com/thebotbites/status/2120289561679163612"}, {"author_id": "757940114949537792", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:50:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120287976412635527"], "id": "2120287976412635527", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind The MKA benchmark in this thread puts Carbon at 56.3% quality, just behind Claude Fable 5.2 at 56.6%, at $5.63 per task versus $35.28 for Fable.", "url": "https://x.com/sulaiman_svesal/status/2120287976412635527"}, {"author_id": "1500400160337235968", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:48:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120287553777729709"], "id": "2120287553777729709", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind @GeminiApp Pitching 'uncovering software vulnerabilities' over footage of a cozy browser tycoon game is classic AI marketing.\n\nEnjoy the unquantized weights on AI Ultra while they last, before unit economics force aggressive FP8 KV cache pruning across the API in a month.", "url": "https://x.com/OLeisgen/status/2120287553777729709"}, {"author_id": "16397411", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:44:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120286478521794767"], "id": "2120286478521794767", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind long-horizon is where most agents drift. curious to see what does carbon does when the plan it started with turns out wrong halfway through", "url": "https://x.com/DomJoLuna/status/2120286478521794767"}, {"author_id": "1687985018717478912", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:21:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120280647537394103"], "id": "2120280647537394103", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind MKA is a welcome benchmark: most real office work is scanned PDFs, invoices and spreadsheets, not clean text. Will it include non-English documents? That's where a lot of agents still break.", "url": "https://x.com/charl1sebastian/status/2120280647537394103"}, {"author_id": "1539244786921635842", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:18:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120279977455476883"], "id": "2120279977455476883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Google DeepMind is telling people to start building with Gemini 4 Carbon. A November market asks whether Carbon reaches the public Gemini API, and whether Anthropic starts trading, both, or neither?\n\nhttps://t.co/pbvRfU1f46", "url": "https://x.com/bwhdx/status/2120279977455476883"}, {"author_id": "2040126646376628225", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:13:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120278823979876850"], "id": "2120278823979876850", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind The verification loops are what I care about. I can't always tell when code is wrong, so a model that checks its own work saves me hours.", "url": "https://x.com/ItsBoban/status/2120278823979876850"}, {"author_id": "2078707395438759936", "conversation_id": "2120219371473617099", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:07:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120277291939123442"], "id": "2120277291939123442", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GoogleDeepMind Extended verification loops are the key claim here. The risk is a model verifying itself into confidence — checking its own output with the same assumptions. External tests, independent tools, and surfacing uncertainty would make this far more usable in real codebases.", "url": "https://x.com/sunder0yct/status/2120277291939123442"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2102064626099699713", "name": "叶子的AI视界", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 7, "following_count": 5, "like_count": 3, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 1, "tweet_count": 30}, "username": "Ian18858863"}, {"id": "1664916049995743232", "name": "Doriana", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 10, "following_count": 14, "like_count": 20, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 5, "tweet_count": 271}, "username": "astierun"}, {"id": "2100257555477868544", "name": "AI Early Edition", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 5, "following_count": 1, "like_count": 17, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 38, "tweet_count": 384